# Tokens for `conditional_headers`. The input is
#   u64 last_modified | u8 flags | u8 pick | if-none-match \0 if-modified-since \0 etag
# so the NUL that ends a field is itself a token worth having: without it
# the fuzzer spends its whole budget inside the If-None-Match field and
# never reaches the date or the server's own entity tag.
"\x00"
"\x00\x00"

# --- If-None-Match, RFC 9110 §13.1.2 --------------------------------
# The list grammar. `*` is the one member that matches without naming
# anything, and the separator is what turns one tag into a list.
"*"
","
", "
" , "
"\x09"

# --- Entity tags, RFC 9110 §8.8.3 ------------------------------------
# The weak prefix is compared away by If-None-Match (and only by it), so
# both spellings of one tag have to be reachable.
"\""
"\"\""
"W/"
"W/\""
"\"abc\""
"W/\"abc\""
# The shape `static_files::etag_for` actually emits: length-mtime, hex.
"\"3e8-6553f100\""
"-"

# --- If-Modified-Since, RFC 9110 §5.6.7 -------------------------------
# All three grammars a recipient must accept, one instant per line, plus
# the pieces a mutant needs to build a near-miss date of its own.
"GMT"
" GMT"
"Sun, 06 Nov 1994 08:49:37 GMT"
"Sunday, 06-Nov-94 08:49:37 GMT"
"Sun Nov  6 08:49:37 1994"
"Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT"
"Tue, 14 Nov 2023 22:13:20 GMT"
"Mon, 29 Feb 2016 12:00:00 GMT"
"Fri, 31 Dec 9999 23:59:59 GMT"
"-Nov-"
"00:00:00"
"23:59:59"
"1970"
"9999"
"Feb"
"Dec"
